This is a greedy construction with a time budget. I have not compiled or run it.

**Approach**
1. Map tags to integer ids and keep each photo's tags as a sorted vector.
2. Pair the vertical photos. Sort them by tag count and pair the i-th smallest with the i-th largest, so the combined tag sets are balanced. A cheaper alternative would be to pair neighbours in sorted order, but balanced pairs tend to give slides with similar sizes. Any pairing is valid. If the number of vertical photos is odd, the leftover one is dropped.
3. Build the slides as sorted tag-id vectors, which are the union of the pair for vertical slides.
4. Order the slides greedily. From the current slide, look at candidate slides that share a tag. Use inverted lists from tag to slides, and limit the number of candidates examined. Pick the candidate with the best interest score among unused ones.
5. To avoid scanning long lists of used slides, keep a per-tag pointer that skips used entries from the front. For each tag in the current slide, scan at most K unused entries from its list. Skipped (used) entries are removed lazily by swapping them out of the list. Tags can be very common, so K is capped at about 30 per tag. Slides have up to 200 tags, giving up to about 6000 candidates per step.
6. Computing the score for a candidate takes a merge of the sorted vectors. Candidates are deduplicated with a stamp array.
7. If no candidate shares a tag, take any unused slide, using a global pointer that advances past used slides.

**Cost**
- Each step touches up to about 6000 candidates, and each score is a merge of about 100 to 200 elements. That is too heavy for 1e5 steps (roughly 1e11 operations).
- To fix this, the per-tag cap becomes `K = max(2, 600 / numtags)` and the total candidates are limited to about 150. Each step then costs about 150 × 100 = 15k operations. Over 1e5 steps that is 1.5e9, which is acceptable.
- I also add a time check. If elapsed time exceeds 7 seconds, the cap is reduced to a few candidates.

**Scan details**
- For each tag in the current slide, iterate its list from the back. Remove used entries by popping them from the back, and examine up to K unused ones from the back. I take the last K entries from the list's tail without removing the unused ones.
- Early exit: if the score reaches `floor(min(|A|,|B|)/2)`-level optimum, stop. This is a simple bound: the score is at most `min(|A|/2, ...)`. I use the bound `|cur|/2` and stop when it is reached.

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main(){
    int n;
    scanf("%d",&n);
    unordered_map<string,int> mp;
    vector<vector<int>> t(n);
    vector<char> o(n);
    char buf[64];
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        int m;
        scanf(" %c %d",&o[i],&m);
        for(int j=0;j<m;j++){
            scanf("%s",buf);
            auto it=mp.emplace(buf,(int)mp.size()).first;
            t[i].push_back(it->second);
        }
        sort(t[i].begin(),t[i].end());
    }
    vector<vector<int>> st;
    vector<array<int,2>> ids;
    vector<int> vs;
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        if(o[i]=='H'){st.push_back(t[i]);ids.push_back({i,-1});}
        else vs.push_back(i);
    }
    stable_sort(vs.begin(),vs.end(),[&](int a,int b){return t[a].size()<t[b].size();});
    int l=0,r=(int)vs.size()-1;
    while(l<r){
        int a=vs[l++],b=vs[r--];
        vector<int> u;
        set_union(t[a].begin(),t[a].end(),t[b].begin(),t[b].end(),back_inserter(u));
        st.push_back(u);
        ids.push_back({a,b});
    }
    int S=st.size();
    int T=mp.size();
    vector<vector<int>> lst(T);
    for(int i=0;i<S;i++)for(int x:st[i])lst[x].push_back(i);
    vector<char> used(S,0);
    vector<int> stamp(S,-1);
    auto score=[&](int a,int b){
        auto&A=st[a];auto&B=st[b];
        int c=0;size_t i=0,j=0;
        while(i<A.size()&&j<B.size()){
            if(A[i]==B[j]){c++;i++;j++;}
            else if(A[i]<B[j])i++;else j++;
        }
        return min(c,min((int)A.size()-c,(int)B.size()-c));
    };
    auto st0=chrono::steady_clock::now();
    vector<int> order;
    if(S==0){printf("1\n0\n");return 0;}
    int cur=0,gp=0;
    used[0]=1;
    order.push_back(0);
    for(int step=1;step<S;step++){
        double el=chrono::duration<double>(chrono::steady_clock::now()-st0).count();
        int total=el>7?10:150;
        int best=-1,bs=-1;
        int cnt=0;
        int opt=st[cur].size()/2;
        auto&C=st[cur];
        int K=max(2,total*4/(int)max<size_t>(1,C.size()));
        for(int x:C){
            auto&L=lst[x];
            while(!L.empty()&&used[L.back()])L.pop_back();
            int seen=0;
            for(int p=(int)L.size()-1;p>=0&&seen<K;p--){
                int c=L[p];
                if(used[c])continue;
                seen++;
                if(stamp[c]==step)continue;
                stamp[c]=step;
                int s=score(cur,c);
                cnt++;
                if(s>bs){bs=s;best=c;}
            }
            if(bs>=opt||cnt>=total)break;
        }
        if(best<0){
            while(used[gp])gp++;
            best=gp;
        }
        used[best]=1;
        order.push_back(best);
        cur=best;
    }
    printf("%d\n",S);
    for(int s:order){
        if(ids[s][1]<0)printf("%d\n",ids[s][0]);
        else printf("%d %d\n",ids[s][0],ids[s][1]);
    }
}
